<title>USA: Travelers 401(k) option plan questioned - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Travelers 401(k) option plan questioned - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Internal Revenue Service is reconsidering a ruling which would have let Travelers Group Inc contribute Travelers stock options to its employees' 401(k) plans, the Wall Street Journal said in Monday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>The paper said the agency declined to comment but cited a government official as saying the IRS was rethinking its private-letter ruling issued on March 21.</p>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department, which was expected to decide on the matter by the end of March, had also not made up its mind on the plan, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>A Labor Department spokeswoman was quoted as saying: &quot;Some concerns have been raised and the Labor Department is considering them.&quot;</p>
<p>Travelers was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
